    "raw_text": "\n<think>\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt. The prompt asks for \"a 15-second, 9:16 vertical video of a real person doing woodworking, with a hammer and wood.\"\n\nLooking at the frames:\n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\n- The frames depict a man in a blue work shirt in what appears to be a workshop setting.\n- Lighting is natural and consistent, coming from a window, producing believable shadows.\n- The image quality is solid overall; there are no major artifacts or distortions, though occasional minor softness may appear in some frames.\n- The framing remains stable and coherent across shots, with good depth cues and texture detail on wood and tools.\n- Overall visual quality is strong but not flawless.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\n- The scene aligns well with the prompt: a real person performing woodworking, using a hammer and wood, in a workshop environment.\n- The framing is generally vertical or near vertical, and the sequence captures the intended activity with clear progression.\n- There may be minor deviations in exact timing or framing details, but they do not significantly detract from alignment.\n\nPhysical Consistency Analysis:\n- Movements and tool handling feel plausible and consistent with woodworking tasks.\n- The hammering action, grip, and body posture are believable, with natural timing and weight transfer.\n- Lighting and shadows support depth and realism; no obvious physics violations are observed.\n- Overall, physical consistency is strong, with only minor refinements possible.\n\nI'll evaluate the video's key aspects systematically. The visual presentation demonstrates solid technical execution, with natural lighting and stable framing contributing to a convincing depiction of woodworking. The alignment between the prompt and the actual content is strong, capturing the essential elements of a real person working with wood and a hammer in a workshop. The physical interactions appear authentic, with movements that respect basic mechanical principles and human biomechanics.\n\nThe video effectively communicates the woodworking process through precise visual storytelling, maintaining coherence across frames while presenting a realistic craftsperson at work.\n\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality: 4\n(2) text-to-video alignment: 4\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency: 4\n"
